.TH ___EVENT_LOOP_DESTROY 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
___event_loop_destroy \- RAII cleanup function for event_loop
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

___event_loop_destroy(event_loop *lp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Static inline function used as the cleanup callback in
event_loop_declare_scoped() and event_loop_construct_scoped(). If
*lp is not EVENT_LOOP_INVALID, calls __event_loop_destroy(*lp) and
sets *lp to EVENT_LOOP_INVALID.

This function is not intended to be called directly; use
event_loop_declare_scoped() or event_loop_construct_scoped()
instead.

Calling __event_loop_destroy on a stale (already destroyed) handle
is a FATAL ERROR (abort()/SIGABRT); see __event_loop_destroy(3).
This is only reachable here if *lp was left holding a stale value
by code outside the normal declare/construct-scoped lifecycle, since
the scoped macros themselves always leave *lp either live or already
EVENT_LOOP_INVALID.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
lp  Pointer to an event_loop variable (must not be NULL).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Compatible with __attribute__((cleanup)) on GCC and Clang.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_declare_scoped (3),
.BR event_loop_construct_scoped (3),
.BR __event_loop_destroy (3),
.BR event_loop_destroy (3)
